atlas optimization-registry-federation

architecture registry-federation
  canonical_name RegistryFederation
  owns RegistryBinding
  owns FederatedProjection
  owns MachineCoverage
  consumes ArchitectureClaim
  consumes AnalysisUniverse
  publishes RegistryBinding
  publishes MachineCoverage
  family optimization
  domain Optimization / Registry federation
  layer governance
  semantic_question Where does authoritative reality for this identity live, and can the atlas reference it without importing ownership of it?
  purpose Answer two different questions separately. The architecture registry answers what has been modeled. The executable registries answer what machinery exists. Federation references one from the other without copying canonical truth, so curing a visibility gap cannot create a second truth.
  maturity architectural
  node_types RegistryBinding
  node_types RegistryKind
  node_types FederatedProjection
  node_types CoverageDimension
  edge_types references
  edge_types implements
  edge_types validates
  edge_types observes
  invariant a binding is REFERENCE_ONLY; it records where authority lives and never relocates it
  invariant design law is owned by the architecture registry; executable presence is owned by the executable registries; whether either is true is owned by evidence
  invariant an architecture claim marked DORMANT never implies its implementation is absent
  invariant an architecture claim marked active never implies an implementation exists
  invariant a definition is referenced, never copied between registries; a copy creates a second truth and is a defect
  invariant atlas validity is one coverage dimension and is never reported as machine completeness
  invariant a federated projection is rebuilt from source digests incrementally, never by rescanning every registry on every invocation
  forbidden_inference an identity being absent from the architecture registry -> that identity being absent from the machine
  forbidden_inference an identity being present in the architecture registry -> an implementation existing
  forbidden_inference a validator existing -> that validator currently passing
  forbidden_inference a validator passing -> the substrate being used by anything
  forbidden_inference architecture record count -> machine completeness
  interacts architecture-claim
  interacts readiness-state
  interacts analysis-universe
  source_path cmd/BonfyreAtlas/src/main.c
  witness bun test architecture/tests/atlas_machine.test.mjs proves bound/unbound accounting, reference-only authority and cache invalidation on lineage changes
  source_lineage Generation-10 registry split discovery, 2026-08-26

  registry_kind design
  path architecture/
  owns design law, semantic intent, topology, lineage, proposals, explanatory structure
  registry_kind canonical-executable
  path .bonfyre/run8/canonical/estate/
  owns executable presence, implementations, validators, runtime contracts, physical bodies
  registry_kind evidence
  path evidence/ and receipts and measurements
  owns whether either of the above is actually true

  binding_field claim_id
  binding_field semantic_identity
  binding_field registry_kind
  binding_field authoritative_source
  binding_field source_path
  binding_field source_digest
  binding_field validator_path
  binding_field evidence_refs
  binding_field relation
  binding_field verification_state
  binding_field observed_at
  binding_field authority

  relation IMPLEMENTS
  relation VALIDATES
  relation MATERIALIZES
  relation PROJECTS
  relation DEPENDS_ON
  relation SUPERSEDES
  relation OBSERVES
  relation BENCHMARKS
  relation DOCUMENTS

  authority REFERENCE_ONLY
  detail The only legal authority value for a binding. Anything else is a copy.

  coverage_dimension design
  question how much intended architecture is represented
  coverage_dimension execution
  question how much known executable machinery is represented
  coverage_dimension binding
  question how much design has a link to implementation
  coverage_dimension verification
  question how much implementation has evidence
  coverage_dimension lineage
  question how much current design preserves origin and corrections
  coverage_dimension runtime
  question how much executable machinery has actually been exercised
  coverage_dimension projection
  question how much executable machinery is reachable from products and surfaces
  coverage_dimension lowering
  question how much repeated semantic work has been lowered

  existence_ladder exists
  existence_ladder validated_historically
  existence_ladder available_on_this_host
  existence_ladder activated
  existence_ladder currently_used
  existence_ladder used_by_a_named_estate
  existence_ladder measured_under_that_estate
  existence_ladder eligible_for_lowering
  existence_ladder_invariant each rung is a separate fact; none implies the next
  existence_ladder_note collapsing these is the largest remaining false-promotion risk

  admission_rule inference-ceiling
  detail A claim whose primary basis is a filename, directory name, job name, route name, derived count, interface label, framing analogy or absence from one registry defaults to ASSERTED_BY_INFERENCE with a promotion ceiling of CANDIDATE.
  raised_by reading the primary source body
  raised_by a runtime observation
  raised_by an authoritative query
  raised_by a validator
  raised_by a receipt
  raised_by an independent reconciliation
  prohibition ASSERTED_BY_INFERENCE alone never justifies creating a semantic owner, removing anything, asserting capability equivalence, eliminating behavior, classifying an effect, assigning authority, lowering, platformizing or retiring
  rationale three retractions in one session, every one an inference from a name or a derived count; an evolutionary optimizer left unbounded would harden its own guesses

interaction federation-bounds-coverage-claims
  source registry-federation
  destination readiness-state
  relation coverage_constraint
  preserves the separation between modeled, implemented, exercised and used
  drops any single completeness number presented as machine state
  forbidden_inference a validating atlas -> a complete machine
